  "id": "COMPOUND:43386 - PROTEIN:5867",
  "verbalization": "Nardostachin is implicated in the pathogenesis of HaCaT cells through a multi-step mechanism involving microtubule-associated protein 1B. This protein is targeted by both Nardostachin and Oleamide, which in turn target HaCaT cells. The presence of multiple pathways converging on microtubule-associated protein 1B suggests a potential role in cellular processes such as proliferation or survival, which could contribute to the observed effects on HaCaT cells. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the interaction, with Nardostachin acting as a direct target for microtubule-associated protein 1B, potentially modulating cellular functions through microtubule dynamics. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Nardostachin and HaCaT, though the exact cellular processes affected remain to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and their shared downstream effect on HaCaT cells underscores the importance of microtubule-associated protein 1B in this relationship.",
